(5791042, 841281, 82749, '<td valign="top">As an entry for the Hate II challenge this works well.  Expression is good, light is dramatic.  How could it be improved from a portrait perspective?  Current DOF emphasizes the mouth and eyes nicely, but I would have liked to see the upper teeth in better focus -- it is possible some selective sharpening would take care of this (admittedly not OK for basic editing for the Hate challenge, but worth a shot for the Portrait side challenge). And perhaps having the inside of the mouth lit up so we can see the uvula hanging down would add even more pop to this.</td>', 'As an entry for the Hate II challenge this works well.  Expression is good, light is dramatic.  How could it be improved from a portrait perspective?  Current DOF emphasizes the mouth and eyes nicely, but I would have liked to see the upper teeth in better focus -- it is possible some selective sharpening would take care of this (admittedly not OK for basic editing for the Hate challenge, but worth a shot for the Portrait side challenge). And perhaps having the inside of the mouth lit up so we can see the uvula hanging down would add even more pop to this.', '2010-01-02 09:02:51.000000', NULL, 0),
(5791578, 841096, 18197, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by deers:</b></div><hr/><i> Confuser, I dont know how you can''t see the hate in the shot. A voodoo doll is to inflict pain and torture the person(s) its made for. Usually out of hated. Just didn''t understand your comment.<br/>My only "eh" about the shot is the setting. Photographically well done, but would have liked the doll placed in a more abysmal a setting. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>This seems too whimsical, maybe too tongue in cheek, to seem hateful to me. I reserve hate for more profound things than a photo popularity contest, I guess. And I suppose you would need to believe in voodoo (I don''t) and its power to inflict real pain or malady on the object of your hatred. Maybe a more abysmal setting <u>would</u> have helped. Or maybe if the doll was in a quantum entanglement with its object ... well, maybe that''s too long to go into. Anyway, good camera work and processing, but don''t deny me my personal reaction to the subject.</td>', 'Originally posted by deers: Confuser, I dont know how you can''t see the hate in the shot. A voodoo doll is to inflict pain and torture the person(s) its made for. Usually out of hated. Just didn''t understand your comment.My only "eh" about the shot is the setting. Photographically well done, but would have liked the doll placed in a more abysmal a setting.   This seems too whimsical, maybe too tongue in cheek, to seem hateful to me. I reserve hate for more profound things than a photo popularity contest, I guess. And I suppose you would need to believe in voodoo (I don''t) and its power to inflict real pain or malady on the object of your hatred. Maybe a more abysmal setting would have helped. Or maybe if the doll was in a quantum entanglement with its object ... well, maybe that''s too long to go into. Anyway, good camera work and processing, but don''t deny me my personal reaction to the subject.', '2010-01-02 16:14:38.000000', NULL, 0),
